Binaural audio: bundled HRTF data
=================================

sadie2_ku100.dcshrtf (generated by scripts/fetch-hrtf.ps1; see docs/BINAURAL_AUDIO.md section 4.1)

  Source:   SADIE II database, subject D1 (Neumann KU100 dummy head), 48 kHz HRIRs (SOFA),
            version v2-2, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.12092466
            Project page: https://www.york.ac.uk/sadie-project/database.html
  Copyright 2018 University of York. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (SADIE_II_LICENSE.txt in this folder).

  Reference: C. Armstrong, L. Thresh, D. Murphy, G. Kearney, "A Perceptual Evaluation of Individual and
  Non-Individual HRTFs: A Case Study of the SADIE II Database", Applied Sciences 8(11):2029, 2018,
  doi:10.3390/app8112029.

  Changes made by DCS Control (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)): the impulse responses were converted to minimum phase with
  separate per-ear onset delays, diffuse-field equalised, normalised so that a sound from straight ahead keeps its
  level, truncated to 128 taps, triangulated and stored in DCS Control's own .dcshrtf format
  (native/binaural/include/hrtf_format.h, converter src/DcsVr.Core/Hrtf).